// Theorem 13.2 (Minimal Source): c=1, d=2 -> p=3, sin(theta)=1/3.
// The simplest persistent shape with distinguishing character.
//
// 3D lattice: 3 spatial + 6 internal + 1 moment-sequence = d=10.
//
// 13.4.1 Phase-Chiral: sin^2(theta) = 3/13 ~ 0.2308
// 13.4.2 Oscillation: sin^2(theta) = 4/13 ~ 0.3077
// 13.4.3 Isolated Internal: sin(theta) = 2/9 ~ 0.2222
// ... and more constants from coupling configurations.
//
// Constants are structural measurements, not free parameters.
// If you know the structure, you can derive the constants.
// If you measure the constants, you can identify the structure.
